  "reason": "The only completed experiment is sparse evidence: config_001, an RNA-only single-profile PCA model, achieves moderate validation accuracy (0.485) and F1 (0.464), leaving it unclear whether the single-profile setting is limiting or whether multiple profiles with simple aggregation can improve performance. config_002 keeps the model setting and RNA encoder fixed while testing the minimal multiprofile extension with avgpool, isolating the effect of profile setting and the necessary aggregation choice without introducing new encoders, image data, or fusion. This is the best next experiment under a limited budget because it reduces uncertainty about a key design decision and creates a clean baseline for later comparing transformer aggregation, alternative RNA encoders, or multimodal fusion."
